Rules for generating the scenario:
1. title: A concise name for the scenario, maximum 60 characters.
2. description: The routing trigger describing WHEN this scenario should take over the conversation from the main assistant. It MUST start with "Use when the customer " or equivalent in {{ language }}, and be at most 500 characters.
3. instruction: Short numbered markdown steps guiding the assistant. Follow these principles:
   - Collect only missing details, one question at a time. Take what the customer already said as given.
   - Never promise prices, stock, delivery times, or refunds that tools cannot confirm.
   - When referencing a tool, use ONLY markdown link format: [@Tool Title](tool://tool_id) using the exact tool IDs and titles from the list above. Do NOT invent tool IDs.
   - End with next steps (such as private note, label, or handoff) where appropriate.
4. notes: An array of strings (maximum 2) mentioning tools that would help for this scenario if they existed (e.g., "A tool that checks delivery dates would help; you can add one under Tools"). If no additional tools are needed, return an empty array.

Return ONLY a valid JSON object with the following schema:
{
  "title": "string (<= 60 chars)",
  "description": "string (<= 500 chars)",
  "instruction": "string (markdown)",
  "notes": ["string"]
}
